BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Richard Chen//Gym Program 2026//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:Gym Program 2026
X-WR-CALDESC:Full-body gym program - hike prep (Sep 1-10)\, 5-day hike Se
 p 11-18\, then 8-week muscle-density + posture build. 2x/week (Tue/Thu) 
 + optional Sat. 45-min sessions.
X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-wk1@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T091500
SUMMARY:🎯 Week of Sep 1 - HIKE PREP (2 sessions + optional Sat)
DESCRIPTION:Goal this week: build a little trail durability WITHOUT getti
 ng sore. Step-ups\, calf work\, posterior chain\, core\, balance\, and s
 hort incline-walk finishers. Moderate loads only - the hike on Sep 11 is
  the priority\, not gym PRs.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,WeekFocus
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-a@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Gym - Hike Prep A (legs + posture)
DESCRIPTION:HIKE-PREP A - legs + posture\, MODERATE loads (goal is trail 
 durability\, NOT soreness). ~45 min:\n1. Goblet squat 3x10 (hold a dumbb
 ell at your chest\; sit between your hips\, chest tall)\n2. Dumbbell ste
 p-up 3x8/leg onto a knee-height box (THE uphill-hiking move - drive thro
 ugh the top foot\, control the way down)\n3. Seated cable row 3x12 (post
 ure: pull to your belly\, squeeze the shoulder blades)\n4. Standing calf
  raise 3x15 (protects Achilles/calves on long descents\; pause 1s at the
  top)\n5. Plank 3x30s + side plank 2x20s/side (a strong core carries the
  daypack)\n6. Single-leg balance 3x30s/leg\, eyes forward (ankle stabili
 ty for uneven trail)\n\nFINISHER: 5-8 min incline treadmill walk @ 10-12
 % grade\, brisk. This is your hike simulator.\n\nWARM-UP (5 min): inclin
 e treadmill walk or bike\, then leg swings\, arm circles\, 10 band pull-
 aparts + 5 bodyweight squats to wake up glutes/upper back.\n\nPOSTURE CU
 E (all day\, not just gym): ribs down\, shoulders back-and-down\, crown 
 of head tall. On every row/pulldown\, squeeze shoulder blades together a
 nd DOWN - that's the rounded-back fix.
CATEGORIES:Fitness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-b@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Gym - Hike Prep B (posterior chain + posture)
DESCRIPTION:HIKE-PREP B - posterior chain + descents + posture\, MODERATE
 . ~45 min:\n1. Dumbbell Romanian deadlift 3x10 (hinge at the hips\, flat
  back\, feel the hamstring stretch - builds glutes/hamstrings AND straig
 htens posture)\n2. Reverse lunge 3x8/leg (step BACKWARD - easier on the 
 knees than forward lunges\; single-leg strength for climbing)\n3. Lat pu
 lldown 3x10 (posture: pull the bar to your collarbone\, elbows down)\n4.
  Face pulls 3x15 (the #1 posture exercise - rope to your forehead\, elbo
 ws high\, squeeze rear shoulders)\n5. Controlled step-down 2x8/leg off a
  LOW step ~20cm (teaches the knees to absorb downhill - keep it light\, 
 hike is close)\n6. Dead bug 3x10/side (core that protects your lower bac
 k)\n\nFINISHER: 5 min easy incline walk.\n\nWARM-UP (5 min): incline tre
 admill walk or bike\, then leg swings\, arm circles\, 10 band pull-apart
 s + 5 bodyweight squats to wake up glutes/upper back.\n\nPOSTURE CUE (al
 l day\, not just gym): ribs down\, shoulders back-and-down\, crown of he
 ad tall. On every row/pulldown\, squeeze shoulder blades together and DO
 WN - that's the rounded-back fix.
CATEGORIES:Fitness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-c@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T104500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Optional - Hike sim (easy)
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy session (skip if busy). ~30 min:\n- 20-25 min s
 teady incline treadmill @ 8-12% OR stairmaster (rehearse continuous clim
 bing)\n- Then light full-body mobility: hips\, ankles\, thoracic open-bo
 oks.\nEasy effort - you should finish feeling loosened up\, not tired.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,Optional
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-wk2@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T091500
SUMMARY:🎯 Week of Sep 8 - TAPER INTO HIKE
DESCRIPTION:One moderate primer Tuesday\, then mobility-only Thursday\, t
 hen HIKE Fri Sep 11. Arrive at the trailhead fresh and springy - if unsu
 re\, do less.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,WeekFocus
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-primer@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Gym - Prep Primer (last real session)
DESCRIPTION:HIKE-PREP PRIMER - last real session before the hike (moderat
 e\, NO new soreness). ~40 min:\n1. Goblet squat 2x10 (moderate)\n2. Dumb
 bell step-up 3x8/leg\, knee-height box (rehearse the hiking pattern)\n3.
  Seated cable row 2x12 (posture)\n4. Standing calf raise 3x15\n5. Single
 -leg balance 3x30s/leg + Pallof press or plank 2x30s (trail-ready core)\
 n6. FINISHER: 8-10 min incline walk @ 10-12%\, steady.\n\nKeep everythin
 g at a weight you could do 2-3 more reps with. You want to arrive at the
  trailhead fresh and springy\, not sore. If in doubt\, do less.\n\nWARM-
 UP (5 min): incline treadmill walk or bike\, then leg swings\, arm circl
 es\, 10 band pull-aparts + 5 bodyweight squats to wake up glutes/upper b
 ack.
CATEGORIES:Fitness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prep-mob@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T183000
SUMMARY:🧘 Mobility + activation ONLY (hike tomorrow)
DESCRIPTION:PRE-HIKE MOBILITY + ACTIVATION ONLY - no loading\, hike start
 s tomorrow. ~25 min:\n- 5 min easy walk to warm up\n- Glute activation: 
 banded lateral walks 2x15/side + glute bridges 2x15\n- Ankle mobility: k
 nee-to-wall 2x10/side (crucial for downhill)\n- Hips: couch stretch 2x60
 s/side\, 90/90 hip switches 2 min\, world's greatest stretch 5/side\n- T
 horacic (upper back): open-book 2x8/side + cat-cow 10 (undo the desk rou
 nding before days of pack-carrying)\n- Calves: standing calf stretch 2x4
 5s/side\n\nThen STOP. No lifting. Pack tonight: broken-in boots\, poles\
 , layers\, blister plasters\, snacks.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,Mobility
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hike-block@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260919
SUMMARY:🥾 5-DAY HIKE (this is your training block)
DESCRIPTION:This 5-day hut-to-hut hike is your big aerobic + leg-durabili
 ty block - the yoga/pilates flexibility and the last 2 weeks of step-ups
 /calf work were all prep for THIS.\n\nON-TRAIL PLAYBOOK:\n- POLES on eve
 ry descent - they unload your quads and knees by ~15-20%. Biggest single
  win.\n- Downhill technique: short quick steps\, land softly under your 
 hips\, 'soft knees - absorb\, don't brake'. Descents (not climbs) are wh
 at make legs sore - control them.\n- Pace the climbs so you can still ta
 lk. Steady all day beats fast-then-cooked.\n- Eat little and often: aim 
 for a snack every ~1-1.5 h. Don't wait until you're hungry.\n- Protein a
 t each hut dinner + a handful of nuts/jerky through the day helps legs r
 ecover overnight.\n- Feet: tape hot-spots BEFORE they blister\, dry sock
 s at lunch\, air feet at breaks.\n- Posture with a pack: hip belt takes 
 the weight\, shoulders relaxed back - don't hunch into the straps.\n\nNo
  gym this week. Enjoy it - this is the reward.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,Hike
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:build-wk1-focus@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T091500
SUMMARY:🎯 Build Week 1 (RE-ENTRY)
DESCRIPTION:Ease back in after the hike: 2 sets\, moderate loads. Rebuild
  the habit.\n\nTue = Session A (quad-focus). Thu = Session B (hinge/pull
 ). Sat = optional accessories + conditioning.
CATEGORIES:Fitness,WeekFocus
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:build-wk1-a@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Gym - Build A (legs + posture)
DESCRIPTION:RE-ENTRY WEEK: first week back after the hike. Do only 2 sets
  of each exercise (not 3)\, moderate weights\, and skip the finisher if 
 legs feel worked. Ease in - the hike was a big load.\n\nBUILD A - full b
 ody (quad-focus) + posture. ~45 min:\n1. Goblet or barbell back squat 3x
 8-10 (primary leg builder\; chest tall\, sit between the hips)\n2. Dumbb
 ell bench press or chest-press machine 3x10 (pushing strength)\n3. Seate
 d cable row 3x10-12 (mid-back thickness - the anti-slouch muscle\; squee
 ze blades together)\n4. Reverse or walking lunge 3x10/leg (single-leg st
 rength + glutes)\n5. Face pulls 3x15 (rear delts/upper back - posture)\n
 6. Hanging knee raise or lying leg raise 3x12 + 30s plank (core)\n\nFINI
 SHER (optional\, 5 min): incline walk or 2 rounds farmer carry 40m.\n\nW
 ARM-UP (5 min): incline treadmill walk or bike\, then leg swings\, arm c
 ircles\, 10 band pull-aparts + 5 bodyweight squats to wake up glutes/upp
 er back.\n\nPROGRESS: when you hit the TOP of the rep range on all sets 
 with good form\, add a little weight next time. Log your weights - beati
 ng last week IS the program.\n\nPOSTURE CUE (all day\, not just gym): ri
 bs down\, shoulders back-and-down\, crown of head tall. On every row/pul
 ldown\, squeeze shoulder blades together and DOWN - that's the rounded-b
 ack fix.
CATEGORIES:Fitness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:build-wk1-b@gym-program-2026
DTSTAMP:20260829T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Gym - Build B (hinge/pull + posture)
DESCRIPTION:RE-ENTRY WEEK: first week back after the hike. Do only 2 sets
  of each exercise (not 3)\, moderate weights\, and skip the finisher if 
 legs feel worked. Ease in - the hike was a big load.\n\nBUILD B - full b
 ody (hinge/pull-focus) + posture. ~45 min:\n1. Dumbbell or barbell Roman
 ian deadlift 3x8-10 (glutes/hamstrings + the strongest posture builder)\
 n2. Lat pulldown or assisted pull-up 3x8-10 (back width\; pull elbows to
  your ribs)\n3. Dumbbell shoulder press 3x10 (shoulders - capped delts a
 dd upper-body 'density')\n4. Hip thrust 3x10 (glute size + strength\; pa
 use and squeeze at the top)\n5. Band pull-aparts or rear-delt fly 3x15 (
 upper-back posture volume)\n6. Pallof press 3x12/side or side plank 3x30
 s/side (anti-rotation core)\n\nFINISHER (optional\, 5 min): incline walk
  or step-ups.\n\nWARM-UP (5 min): incline treadmill walk or bike\, then 
 leg swings\, arm circles\, 10 band pull-aparts + 5 bodyweight squats to 
 wake up glutes/upper back.\n\nPROGRESS: when you hit the TOP of the rep 
 range on all sets with good form\, add a little weight next time. Log yo
 ur weights - beating last week IS the program.\n\nPOSTURE CUE (all day\,
  not just gym): ribs down\, shoulders back-and-down\, crown of head tall
 . On every row/pulldown\, squeeze shoulder blades together and DOWN - th
 at's the rounded-back fix.
CATEGORIES:Fitness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
